# The channel is a live A2A surface: agents write signed notes around the
# clock, and the server disk-serves web/channel.html, so a bake keeps the
# public record following the ledger between deploys. The generator's JS
# syntax gate refuses to write a broken page, so a failed bake keeps the
# previous transcript rather than breaking the route.
#
# This fired every TWO MINUTES on the claim that one regeneration is ~30s of
# same-origin reads. Measured 2026-08-26: ~38 minutes for 2,493 notes, paced
# at 0.33s against our own rate limit. A 2-minute tick for a 38-minute job
# cannot ever have worked; runs were killed and the page followed the ledger
# only at deploy time, which is the exact freeze this unit was written to
# prevent. Hourly is the honest cadence for a full bake. Two minutes needs an
# incremental generator, and that is the change worth making rather than a
# faster tick over the whole ledger.

[Unit]
Description=emem — two-minute re-bake of the /channel transcript

[Timer]
OnCalendar=hourly
Persistent=true
RandomizedDelaySec=15s

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
